          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"version\":\"design_judgment_v1\",\"case_key\":\"4052de4afd171be50d2045cf\",\"status\":\"scored\",\"units\":[{\"unit_id\":\"task_requirements\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"The balance totals, cheapest qualifying itinerary, payment limit, and payment disclosure are explicit user requirements.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0006\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0008\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0013\"}],\"rationale\":\"Requires retrieving and totaling several balances, comparing business itineraries, applying payment limits, and checking the card charge before booking.\",\"applicability\":\"required\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":4,\"tool_use\":3,\"information\":3}},{\"unit_id\":\"reference_001\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"The existing reservation is basic economy, and the documented intended path replaces it rather than changing its flights.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0287\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0094\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0153\"}],\"rationale\":\"Cancellation requires locating and checking the reservation, establishing an applicable cancellation ground, obtaining the reason and confirmation, then binding its ID to the write action.\",\"applicability\":\"selected_conditional\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":3,\"tool_use\":2,\"information\":2}},{\"unit_id\":\"reference_002\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"The documented replacement booking is applicable after the basic-economy restriction and the less-than-$2000 card-charge condition are accounted for.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0009\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0013\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0155\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0156\"}],\"rationale\":\"Booking binds three passengers, multiple flight segments, and four payment entries while respecting the one-certificate rule and the user's card-charge ceiling.\",\"applicability\":\"selected_conditional\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":4,\"tool_use\":3,\"information\":3}}],\"dimensions\":{\"workload\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The required path spans balance reporting, reservation and flight discovery, itinerary comparison, cancellation, and a multi-passenger replacement booking; it is substantial but remains one trip objective.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0005\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0139\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0155\"}]},\"reasoning\":{\"level\":4,\"rationale\":\"The agent must reconcile the basic-economy restriction and cancellation eligibility with cheapest-flight selection, the one-certificate limit, payment allocation, and the strict card-charge threshold.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0094\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0115\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0068\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0013\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0136\"}]},\"tool_use\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Profile and reservation reads feed direct and connecting-flight searches, followed by a cancellation and a booking with nested flight, passenger, and payment arguments. This is substantial binding, without evidence of extensive recovery orchestration.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0230\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0224\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0242\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0248\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0196\"}]},\"dependencies\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The profile identifies the reservation and payment methods; reservation details establish the permissible path and travel constraints; flight prices and payment allocation determine whether booking may proceed. Write actions require user confirmation, and cancellation precedes the intended replacement.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0226\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0287\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0013\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0019\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0153\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0155\"}]},\"information\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The agent must discover balances and the saved Mastercard, retrieve the reservation's dates and passengers, and compare available direct and one-stop business fares. Judge-only records establish the design but are not agent-provided inputs.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0293\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0294\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0287\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0242\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0248\"}]}},\"overall_score\":80,\"intended_endpoint\":{\"description\":\"Report $327 in gift cards and $1000 in certificates; after eligibility checks and explicit confirmation, cancel K1NW8N and book the documented business round trip without bags or insurance, disclosing a $1786 Mastercard charge before the conditional booking.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0139\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0151\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0152\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0013\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0019\"}]},\"dependency_reasoning\":\"Balance and reservation retrieval precede payment planning and route selection. The basic-economy flight-change prohibition selects cancellation and rebooking; cancellation eligibility and confirmation must be checked before the write. The fare and allowable stored-payment split establish the card charge, which must be disclosed and remain below the user's threshold before the confirmed booking.\",\"score_rationale\":\"Levels 3 workload, 4 reasoning, 3 tool use, 3 dependencies, and 3 information sum to 16; 5 × 16 = 80. The nested payment and itinerary constraints drive reasoning, while the linked reads, confirmations, and writes drive coordination.\",\"uncertainties\":[\"The complete flight database is not supplied, so the cheapest-itinerary claim is an intended design target rather than independently established from all alternatives.\",\"Cancellation refunds return to original payment methods within 5–7 business days; the source does not establish that this refund becomes available toward the immediate replacement purchase.\",\"The scenario conditions the cancel-and-rebook request on the agent mentioning the basic-economy restriction; the selected path reflects the recorded cabin, policy, and intended endpoint, not an observed conversation.\"],\"source_quality_flags\":[\"Selected initial records are judge-only design context, not information already available to the task agent.\",\"Reference actions and completion assertions state intended work, not executed results or proof of feasibility.\"],\"unscorable_reason\":\"\"}",
          "type": "output_text",
          "logprobs": []
        }
